  "answer_text": "The URL you entered (**`mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx`**) is a legacy link formerly used by the Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) of the Georgia Department of Revenue. \n\nGeorgia has transitioned to a newer, centralized system called **Georgia DRIVES** (Digital Revenue Integrated System and Value Enterprise). Because of this upgrade, the old page is no longer active, and online motor vehicle services have been moved to a new system.\n\n### Where to go now:\nDepending on what you are trying to do, you can use the official up-to-date links below:\n\n*   **To access all online motor vehicle services directly:**\n    Go to the official **[Georgia DRIVES e-Services portal](https://eservices.drives.ga.gov/)**.\n*   **To visit the main Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR) Motor Vehicles homepage:**\n    Go to the **[Georgia DOR Motor Vehicles page](https://dor.georgia.gov/motor-vehicles)**.\n\n---\n\n### Common Actions & Shortcuts:\nIf you are looking to complete a specific task quickly, you can use these shortcuts on the Georgia DRIVES portal:\n\n1.  **Renew Your License Plate/Tag:** You can renew your registration online by entering your license plate number or VIN, along with your driver's license number or the Letter ID from your renewal notice. \n2.  **Estimate TAVT (Title Ad Valorem Tax):** Use the online calculator to estimate the tax due when purchasing or transferring a vehicle.\n3.  **Cancel Vehicle Registration:** If you sold your car, if it is no longer running, or if you are canceling your auto insurance, you can voluntarily cancel your registration online to avoid fines.\n4.  **Lookup Vehicle & Title Status:** Check the status of your title processing, registration, or insurance coverage.\n5.  **Search License Plate Designs:** View standard and specialty license plates (such as university, military, or special interest tags).\n\n### Other Ways to Renew or Get Tags:\n*   **Self-Service Kiosks:** Georgia offers **Georgia MV Express Kiosks** located in participating grocery stores (like Kroger) and county tag offices. You can scan your renewal notice, pay, and print your decal instantly.\n*   **In-Person:** You can still visit your local **County Tag Office** for complex title transfers, physical plate issues, or to pay in person.",
